WEBVTT

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:05.350
Chapter 1. Data Storage and Memory.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.575
Computer memory is like the computer's brain.

00:00:10.925 --> 00:00:13.725
It helps the computer to remember things.

00:00:14.075 --> 00:00:17.597
Just like we remember our favourite stories or games,

00:00:17.597 --> 00:00:21.850
the computer needs memory to remember its tasks and information.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.600
Learning Outcomes.

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:29.275
Understand the meaning of data and information.

00:00:29.625 --> 00:00:32.675
Know about computer memory and its types.

00:00:33.025 --> 00:00:36.700
Learn types of storage devices and their uses.

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:43.814
Tia, Have you ever wondered how a computer remembers all our games and pictures?

00:00:44.164 --> 00:00:48.577
I'm not sure, Niha. How does it do that?

00:00:48.927 --> 00:00:54.790
Well, it's like how we keep our toys safe in boxes, a computer has a storage place.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:01:03.154
Oh, I get it, Niha. So, the computer has special places to keep its things?

00:01:03.504 --> 00:01:07.569
Exactly, Tia! We'll learn more about it and how it works.

00:01:07.919 --> 00:01:13.836
That sounds interesting, Niha. Let's explore it together!

00:01:15.686 --> 00:01:17.911
Data vs Information

00:01:18.261 --> 00:01:21.961
Data refers to raw facts in unprocessed form.

00:01:22.311 --> 00:01:25.561
The word "data" is a plural form of "datum".

00:01:25.911 --> 00:01:31.386
When data is processed, organized, structured or presented in a meaningful way,

00:01:31.386 --> 00:01:33.811
then it is called as "Information".

00:01:35.661 --> 00:01:38.036
It is not enough to have data.

00:01:38.386 --> 00:01:40.811
Data themselves is useless.

00:01:41.161 --> 00:01:46.936
But when this data is processed, it becomes useful and can be called as Information.

00:01:48.786 --> 00:01:50.361
Example

00:01:50.711 --> 00:01:54.311
We know that CPU is the brain of a computer.

00:01:54.661 --> 00:01:58.011
It controls all the functions of a computer.

00:01:58.361 --> 00:02:01.411
It processes data and gives results.

00:02:03.261 --> 00:02:06.586
Computers can store large amounts of data.

00:02:06.936 --> 00:02:09.811
We can retrieve the data as we need it.

00:02:11.661 --> 00:02:13.161
MEMORY

00:02:13.511 --> 00:02:17.436
Computer memory is very similar to the human brain.

00:02:17.786 --> 00:02:21.811
It is used to store data and instructions given to it.

00:02:22.161 --> 00:02:26.636
It can store the information either temporarily or permanently.

00:02:28.486 --> 00:02:33.411
In computers, memory is a device that is used to store information.

00:02:33.761 --> 00:02:37.061
A computer can store the program in its memory.

00:02:37.411 --> 00:02:40.367
When a certain program starts on the computer,

00:02:40.367 --> 00:02:43.836
first of all, it is loaded into the computer's memory.

00:02:44.186 --> 00:02:47.636
A computer can load many programs in its memory.

00:02:49.486 --> 00:02:54.687
Faster the memory of the computer is, faster is the speed of opening of the

00:02:54.687 --> 00:02:55.311
programs.

00:02:57.161 --> 00:02:58.736
Example

00:02:59.086 --> 00:03:03.586
Now, we will learn about memory and various storage devices.

00:03:05.436 --> 00:03:07.161
TYPES OF MEMORY

00:03:07.511 --> 00:03:11.661
The computer memory can be classified into the following types:

00:03:13.511 --> 00:03:15.261
Primary memory

00:03:15.611 --> 00:03:17.436
Secondary memory

00:03:19.286 --> 00:03:21.761
Primary or Internal memory

00:03:22.111 --> 00:03:26.836
Primary memory is also known as the internal or main memory.

00:03:27.186 --> 00:03:30.861
A computer cannot run without the primary memory.

00:03:31.211 --> 00:03:37.445
It is used to store data or information that the CPU needs to access directly and

00:03:37.445 --> 00:03:38.061
quickly.

00:03:39.911 --> 00:03:43.611
The Primary memory can be divided into two parts

00:03:43.961 --> 00:03:46.336
RAM (Random Access Memory)

00:03:46.686 --> 00:03:48.786
ROM (Read only Memory)

00:03:50.636 --> 00:03:52.136
RAM

00:03:52.486 --> 00:03:57.811
When we refer to the computer's primary memory, we actually refer to RAM.

00:03:58.161 --> 00:04:02.236
It is used by the computer to store data for processing.

00:04:02.586 --> 00:04:07.311
If the computer is switched off, the data in RAM will be lost.

00:04:07.661 --> 00:04:11.836
Hence, RAM is referred to as volatile memory.

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:15.061
ROM

00:04:15.411 --> 00:04:20.916
It stores permanent instructions required for the proper functioning of a computer

00:04:20.916 --> 00:04:21.386
system.

00:04:21.736 --> 00:04:26.061
These instructions are stored by the manufacturer of the computer.

00:04:26.411 --> 00:04:31.275
ROM is a non-volatile memory, as data stored in it is not lost,

00:04:31.275 --> 00:04:34.286
even when the computer is switched off.

00:04:36.136 --> 00:04:37.961
Secondary Memory

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:41.736
The primary memory is limited and temporary.

00:04:42.086 --> 00:04:47.144
Therefore, there is a need for secondary memory that can be used to store large

00:04:47.144 --> 00:04:48.936
amounts of data permanently.

00:04:49.286 --> 00:04:54.086
The data remains there even when the power to the computer is switched off.

00:04:55.936 --> 00:05:00.111
Some commonly used secondary storage device are as follows

00:05:00.461 --> 00:05:02.061
Hard Disk

00:05:02.411 --> 00:05:04.111
Compact Disc

00:05:04.461 --> 00:05:07.286
DVD (Digital Versatile Disk)

00:05:07.636 --> 00:05:09.236
Pen drive

00:05:09.586 --> 00:05:11.286
Memory Card

00:05:13.136 --> 00:05:14.736
Hard Disk

00:05:15.086 --> 00:05:19.036
A hard disk is the main secondary storage device.

00:05:19.386 --> 00:05:23.736
A hard disk is a device fixed inside the CPU box.

00:05:24.086 --> 00:05:26.811
It can store a huge amount of data.

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:32.611
All the work done on a computer can be stored on a hard disk.

00:05:32.961 --> 00:05:37.361
We can read and write data on this device any number of times.

00:05:39.211 --> 00:05:41.086
TYPES OF HARD DISKS

00:05:41.436 --> 00:05:44.061
Let us see different types of hard disks.

00:05:45.911 --> 00:05:47.836
INTERNAL HARD DISK

00:05:48.186 --> 00:05:53.767
The internal hard disk is the main secondary storage device that is permanently

00:05:53.767 --> 00:05:55.886
installed inside the computer.

00:05:56.236 --> 00:06:01.223
It can store a huge amount of data that includes the operating system,

00:06:01.223 --> 00:06:05.069
application programs and other data, including images,

00:06:05.069 --> 00:06:08.061
documents, music and videos on a computer.

00:06:08.411 --> 00:06:12.363
The hard disk is usually given a label such as C:

00:06:12.363 --> 00:06:15.186
or D: called as C drive or D drive.

00:06:17.036 --> 00:06:18.911
EXTERNAL HARD DISK

00:06:19.261 --> 00:06:25.411
An external hard disk is a removable hard disk that connects to a computer through a

00:06:25.411 --> 00:06:26.436
USB connector.

00:06:26.786 --> 00:06:32.429
You can plug in an external hard disk into multiple computers and use it as a

00:06:32.429 --> 00:06:34.261
removable storage device.

00:06:34.611 --> 00:06:39.786
An external hard disk is, however, slower than an internal hard disk.

00:06:41.636 --> 00:06:43.086
CD

00:06:43.436 --> 00:06:46.911
A compact disc is a type of optical media.

00:06:47.261 --> 00:06:50.661
It can store up to 700 MB of data.

00:06:51.011 --> 00:06:56.603
These are circular in shape and are used mainly for storing audio-visual data in

00:06:56.603 --> 00:06:57.511
digital form.

00:06:59.361 --> 00:07:00.936
DVD

00:07:01.286 --> 00:07:07.715
DVD is another type of optical media used for storing digital data such as videos,

00:07:07.715 --> 00:07:09.361
movies and softwares.

00:07:09.711 --> 00:07:15.236
It is similar to a CD, but it can store ten times more data than a CD.

00:07:15.586 --> 00:07:20.936
The video quality of a DVD is also much better than that of a CD.

00:07:22.786 --> 00:07:24.361
Pendrive

00:07:24.711 --> 00:07:30.596
A pendrive is a storage device which is small in size and can be easily carried in a

00:07:30.596 --> 00:07:31.086
pocket.

00:07:31.436 --> 00:07:34.186
It can store large amounts of data.

00:07:34.536 --> 00:07:39.947
It is mostly used to transfer data quickly and efficiently from one computer to

00:07:39.947 --> 00:07:41.111
another computer.

00:07:41.461 --> 00:07:47.445
It has to be inserted into a computer's USB port to store or retrieve information

00:07:47.445 --> 00:07:48.036
from it.

00:07:49.886 --> 00:07:51.586
Memory Card

00:07:51.936 --> 00:07:56.186
A memory card is a very small compact storage device.

00:07:56.536 --> 00:07:59.825
It is mainly used in cameras, music players,

00:07:59.825 --> 00:08:03.487
and smartphones to store pictures, songs, movies,

00:08:03.487 --> 00:08:03.786
etc.

00:08:05.636 --> 00:08:07.336
MEMORY UNITS

00:08:07.686 --> 00:08:11.986
Data stored in the memory is measured in the units such as bits,

00:08:11.986 --> 00:08:16.286
bytes, kilobytes, megabytes, gigabytes, terabytes and petabytes.

00:08:16.636 --> 00:08:22.286
Bit: A bit (short for binary digit) is the smallest unit of data in a computer.

00:08:22.636 --> 00:08:26.761
A bit has a single binary value, either 0 or 1.

00:08:28.611 --> 00:08:31.186
Byte: Combination of 8 bits.

00:08:31.536 --> 00:08:35.511
One byte stores one character such as any letter 'k',

00:08:35.511 --> 00:08:38.436
'a' or any other symbol like @, $, etc.

00:08:40.286 --> 00:08:41.711
Nibble

00:08:42.061 --> 00:08:44.811
Half a byte (four bits) is called Nibble.

00:08:45.161 --> 00:08:50.911
The bits in a byte are normally numbered from zero to seven using the convention as

00:08:50.911 --> 00:08:51.811
shown below :

00:08:53.661 --> 00:08:56.011
MEASURING THE COMPUTER'S MEMORY

00:08:56.361 --> 00:08:59.261
One file can be of thousands of bytes.

00:08:59.611 --> 00:09:02.599
So, instead of using bytes to measure data,

00:09:02.599 --> 00:09:05.865
we can also use higher units such as kilobytes,

00:09:05.865 --> 00:09:09.061
megabytes, gigabytes, terabytes and petabytes.

00:09:09.411 --> 00:09:13.886
Both computer memory and disk space are measured in these units.

00:09:15.736 --> 00:09:19.311
1 Bit = Binary Digit (0 or 1)

00:09:19.661 --> 00:09:21.936
1 Byte = 8 Bits

00:09:22.286 --> 00:09:26.361
1024 Bytes = 1 Kilo Byte

00:09:26.711 --> 00:09:31.711
1024 Kilo Bytes (KB) = 1 Mega Byte

00:09:32.061 --> 00:09:36.686
1024 Mega Bytes (MB) = 1 Giga Byte

00:09:38.536 --> 00:09:43.611
1024 Giga Bytes (GB) = 1 Tera Byte

00:09:43.961 --> 00:09:48.936
1024 Tera Bytes (TB) = 1 Peta Byte

00:09:49.286 --> 00:09:54.236
1024 Peta Bytes (PB) = 1 Exa Byte

00:09:54.586 --> 00:09:59.511
1024 Exa Bytes (EB) = 1 Zetta Byte

00:09:59.861 --> 00:10:04.886
1024 Zetta Bytes (ZB) = 1 Yotta Byte

00:10:06.736 --> 00:10:11.936
You enter data and instruction into the computer using input devices.

00:10:12.286 --> 00:10:18.111
The data and instructions are stored inside the computer in some storage devices.

00:10:18.461 --> 00:10:22.936
Primary memory and secondary memory are the two types of memory.

00:10:23.286 --> 00:10:30.561
Some commonly used secondary devices are Hard disk, Pen drive, DVD, CD, etc.

00:10:30.911 --> 00:10:35.261
Primary memory is of two types- RAM and ROM.

00:10:35.611 --> 00:10:39.986
The data stored on the computers is handled in terms of bits.
